{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules","id":1443232,"title":"WtA 20th Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-09T02:57:28-07:00","id":1443232,"title":"WtA 20th Rules","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I'm prepping to run my first WtA game and currently I'm using WtA 20th.<br /> <br /> Now cWoD rules aren't always the best, I know that, but the WtA 20s layout and writing are just horrible so far.<br /> I found that rules are all over the place and also not very clear in many cases... is revised any better in that regard? (for example the rage effect &quot;The Curse&quot; is not listed with here is what rage does, it in a whole other chapter. Also not sure if it refers to permanent or temporary rage)<br /> And many of the gifts are very murky, don't provide any real rules and in some cases let you do a thing that I thought you would be able to do in the exact or almost exact same way without a gift. (looking at you Sense Prey, or hell, the level THREE gift Pathfinder... just to give some examples)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Ancestor and Fate Backgrounds, sooo am I reading those wrong or do they, mechanically speaking, do the exact same thing only fate is just way better. Both essentially give you extra dice on a roll once per session. But with Ancestor you have to decide to do so before the roll, with Fate you can do so after you failed the roll. With Ancestor you roll your rating against diff 8 or 10! and then add any successes as a bonus dice to your roll. With fate just roll the rating against diff 8 and any successes simply adds a successes to your initial roll...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Spirits:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Materialize seems to be missing something? As written, a spirit can just do it whenever it wants as long as the Gauntlet rating isn't to high. But the Wyrmhole writeup seems to suggest that there is a cost to Materialize. Also how many health levels does a materialized Spirit get.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Similar Possession, all the fluff suggests that Wyrm aligned entities do a lot to make people more susceptible to Possession. But in the rules for Possession, a spirit with the charm can simply use it on anyone and with a Gnosis 3 or 4 should have a very good chance to possess pretty much any mortal.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">What really makes me wonder if I understand thing correctly is when I look at the stats and abilities of the mighty Nexus Crawler. It seems to that any half way descent Werewolf pack wouldn't have to hard a time to defeat a single one. Am I missing something?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Sorry if that post has been a bit of mix of ranting and actual questions, but currently I'm just frustrated with the rulebook... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T05:15:07-07:00","id":1443246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules#post1443232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is revised any better in that regard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules#post1443232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (for example the rage effect &quot;The Curse&quot; is not listed with here is what rage does, it in a whole other chapter. Also not sure if it refers to permanent or temporary rage)</div> </div> </div> </div>Permanent, usually. Even better, not all the options you have with spending Rage are detailed with Rage, but some are in the combat chapter.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules#post1443232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And many of the gifts are very murky, don't provide any real rules and in some cases let you do a thing that I thought you would be able to do in the exact or almost exact same way without a gift. (looking at you Sense Prey, or hell, the level THREE gift Pathfinder... just to give some examples)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. Sone gifts are magical senses that defy the somewhat vague rules of natural senses. So, Sense Prey would be a magical sense to find prey animals, that you wouldn't find with natural senses, then again, if the garou could read, it could find an animal shelter, farm or zoo by itself, too.<br /> Same goes for Pathfinder. Sure, running parcour alone would possibly yield some benefit, but this gifts works in unfamiliar territory and without considerable athletics skill, either. So it is kinda magic, but still something not to fancy...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules#post1443232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancestor and Fate Backgrounds, sooo am I reading those wrong or do they, mechanically speaking, do the exact same thing only fate is just way better. Both essentially give you extra dice on a roll once per session. But with Ancestor you have to decide to do so before the roll, with Fate you can do so after you failed the roll. With Ancestor you roll your rating against diff 8 or 10! and then add any successes as a bonus dice to your roll. With fate just roll the rating against diff 8 and any successes simply adds a successes to your initial roll...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate can be pooled for the whole pack. Ancestors can also give specific advice and precognition about decisions at the stroyteller's discretion. So, it is more versatile.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules#post1443232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Materialize seems to be missing something? As written, a spirit can just do it whenever it wants as long as the Gauntlet rating isn't to high. But the Wyrmhole writeup seems to suggest that there is a cost to Materialize. Also how many health levels does a materialized Spirit get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, materialize is cost free since 2nd Edition. Possibly the wyrmhole author didn't know that or tried to answer questions nobody would ever ask...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules#post1443232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar Possession, all the fluff suggests that Wyrm aligned entities do a lot to make people more susceptible to Possession. But in the rules for Possession, a spirit with the charm can simply use it on anyone and with a Gnosis 3 or 4 should have a very good chance to possess pretty much any mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, rules and fluff often don't make a lot of sense. Even with medium to high willpower a bane could easily possess a human, permanently, within six hours. Why don't they? Well, they seem to be choosy on whom they possess, I guess.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules#post1443232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What really makes me wonder if I understand thing correctly is when I look at the stats and abilities of the mighty Nexus Crawler. It seems to that any half way descent Werewolf pack wouldn't have to hard a time to defeat a single one. Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the stats are fine and one has to destroy 30 to 100 Essence, which ca be a lot, or 12 health levels when materialized, which is nothing. Problem is the &quot;Alter reality&quot; Charm with vague guidelines on how any alteration affects the attackers or the environment. 6 dice of willpower against diff 7 seems easily enough, but a lot of successes aren't that likely. Why it rolles Willpower (the trait for physical feats of spirits) and not Gnosis (the trait for mental and social feats for spirits) will remain a mystery. Possibly the spirit has to use his legs to physically alter the reality?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules#post1443232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if that post has been a bit of mix of ranting and actual questions, but currently I'm just frustrated with the rulebook... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you aren't the first...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T05:59:26-07:00","id":1443249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules?p=1443246#post1443246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really.<br /> Permanent, usually. Even better, not all the options you have with spending Rage are detailed with Rage, but some are in the combat chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Interesting, which means most Ahroun and Galliard couldn't interact with many/most humans at all. Which again seems to be at odds with the fluff^^, but well... I might houserule that to temporary Rage</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T06:25:38-07:00","id":1443253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1443232-wta-20th-rules?p=1443249#post1443249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, which means most Ahroun and Galliard couldn't interact with many/most humans at all. Which again seems to be at odds with the fluff^^, but well... I might houserule that to temporary Rage</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the rules for the Curse are somewhat problematic, regarding the supposed willpower of average humans and the Rage traits characters start with. There are Gifts in some editions, that mitigate the effects of Rage in regards to the Curse.<br /> With the Curses effect not just displeasure, distrust, uneasiness and fear near such garou, but outright panic, as in running away from one's place of work screaming, is bordering slapstick comedy. I mean, you enter a pit stop to pay for gas and get some gum and the cashier runs away screaming, with a unexplained rush of panic.<br /> You could always escalate to some drama, but it does distract from the story at hand, doesn't it?<br /> In 2nd Edition there were proper dice rolls to check how log-term interaction with humans would fail. Game designers should have expanded on that and toned down the immediate effects of the Curse...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 04-09-2021, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}